<report>
<title>Analysis of variance from regression</title>
<table>
<tr><th>Source of variation</th><th>Sum Squares</th><th>DF</th><th>Mean Square</th></tr>
<tr><td>Regression</td><td>@reg_sum</td><td>@reg_df</td><td>@reg_mean</td></tr>
<tr><td>Residual</td><td>@res_sum</td><td>@res_df</td><td>@res_mean</td></tr>
<tr><td><grandtotal>Total (corrected)</grandtotal></td><td><grandtotal>@tot_sum</grandtotal></td><td><grandtotal>@tot_df</grandtotal></td><td></td></tr>
</table>

<p>Root MSE = @mse</p>

<p>F = @f <pval>@{p:pval}</pval></p>

<table>
<tr><td>Multiple correlation coefficient</td><td>(R) = @r</td></tr>
<tr><td></td><td>R&#xb2;  = @r2</td></tr>
<tr><td></td><td>Ra&#xb2; = @ra2</td></tr>
</table>

<p>Durbin-Watson test statistic = @dw</p>
</report>
